WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.970
- Something we do have in common,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.570
my mother and I actually
have in common as well,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.980
we read a lot of books together,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.360
and you love, you're
an avid reader as well.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.230
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.810
- So, I mean, are you
currently reading anything cool

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.790
I should know about?

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.480
- Well, I'm reading "Caste."

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.430
It's kind of heavy,

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.930
so I have to just read
a little bit at a time.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.810
You just can't sit there
and read the whole book.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.580
But what are you reading?

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.490
- I just, well, I just
read your book actually,

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.134
but I also read I think
it's "The Dutch House?"

00:00:25.134 --> 00:00:26.130
Ann Patchett?
- Oh yeah, I've read that!

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:26.963
Oh, you did?
- Oh,

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:28.080
- don't you love Ann Patchett?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.080
- I love when you find an author you love

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.340
that really captivates you

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.130
and keeps you kind of
enthralled in the book.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.690
- She did one of my book talks,

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.130
and I loved her so much that I invited her

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:41.060
to come to the vice president's
residence and she came!

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.170
And so that was so neat
to get to meet her,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.800
and it's so nice when you
get to meet these people

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.270
who are, you know, your idols,

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.570
and as an English teacher,
of course, you know,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.990
I love authors, so.
- Yeah!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.055
- [Kelly] Yeah, that is nice perk.

00:00:53.055 --> 00:00:54.730
- And she has her own
bookstore, you know that.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.540
- Yes, yes, I did, I did.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.700
And I think that's gotta be

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.040
one of the coolest perks of this job.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.090
You're like, hey, you want to come

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.492
swing by the White House and hang out?

00:01:02.492 --> 00:01:03.325
(Kelly laughs)
(Jill laughs)

00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:04.540
And then they do!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.840
- Yeah, yeah.
- That's incredible.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.050
- And actually it's funny,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.330
that's why, I'm a singer
first and foremost,

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.060
but I, you know, I
signed up to do this job,

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.910
and I get to meet so
many incredible people.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.820
So it's kind of a similar thing.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.100
I get to interview so
many people that I idolize

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.690
and look up to and I'm inspired by.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.883
So it's a really cool thing, I agree.

